{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550472-vtm-with-covenant","id":1550472,"title":"VtM with Covenant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-28T22:17:07-07:00","id":1550472,"title":"VtM with Covenant","content":"I'm sure it's been asked, but has anyone used Covenants from VtR in VtM? If so how did it work, like it, dislike it? High points? Problems? Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T09:35:45-07:00","id":1550482,"title":"","content":"Do you mean adding the Covenants to the sects already existing in VtM lore and setting? That sounds a bit messy and overcrowded if I'm honest.<br /> <br /> Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs, Inconnu, Tal'Maje'Ra, Banu Haqim, Giovanni/Hecate, Setites, Ashirra and all their subdivisions, plus less identifiable groupings like the Ebony Kingdom, Kuei Jin, Drowned Legacies... It's already a lot. Sure, some groups can be reframed as <i>parts of </i>Invictus, Ordo Dracul, Lancea Sanctum, Carthian Movement and Circle of the Crone... but why?<br /> <br /> Or did I misunderstand your question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T12:35:53-07:00","id":1550489,"title":"","content":"I've used stuff from the 1st ed Invictus and Carthean books to flesh out my own versions of the Camarilla and Anarchs respectively, and stuff from the LS and Crone books for aspects of Kindred religion. But the only one I have tried using as its own thing was the Ordo Dracul as a mystery cult. It worked fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T20:08:22-07:00","id":1550498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550472-vtm-with-covenant?p=1550482#post1550482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean adding the Covenants to the sects already existing in VtM lore and setting? That sounds a bit messy and overcrowded if I'm honest.<br /> <br /> Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs, Inconnu, Tal'Maje'Ra, Banu Haqim, Giovanni/Hecate, Setites, Ashirra and all their subdivisions, plus less identifiable groupings like the Ebony Kingdom, Kuei Jin, Drowned Legacies... It's already a lot. Sure, some groups can be reframed as <i>parts of </i>Invictus, Ordo Dracul, Lancea Sanctum, Carthian Movement and Circle of the Crone... but why?<br /> <br /> Or did I misunderstand your question?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you got it right, but dont always use those others, on grand scale yea they are there. But how would one of those work in a setting, maybe not all of them there or even all of them exist in VtM. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T20:12:21-07:00","id":1550499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550472-vtm-with-covenant?p=1550489#post1550489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've used stuff from the 1st ed Invictus and Carthean books to flesh out my own versions of the Camarilla and Anarchs respectively, and stuff from the LS and Crone books for aspects of Kindred religion. But the only one I have tried using as its own thing was the Ordo Dracul as a mystery cult. It worked fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats awesome, I was considering adding The Carthian Movement as a faction in the Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T12:57:22-07:00","id":1550601,"title":"","content":"You may want to check out the <a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a> VtM chronicle site on Obsidian Portal done by board member <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3110_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3110\" data-vbnamecard=\"3110\">False Epiphany</a>. It integrates a lot of Requiem concepts into the Masquerade setting. Essentially most of the covenants are for vampires within the Camarilla, and the Carthians are mostly turned into anarchs. He incorporated Requiem's New Orleans City of the Damned sourcebook into the Masquerade setting, but I think he modified a lot of the behind the scenes secrets and lore plus threw in a bunch of Masquerade canon to augment things. For example, he moved a lot of characters from the Masquerade New Orleans by Night to Baton Rouge so they exist in some capacity.<br /> <br /> The amount of work reconciling the two setting is impressive.<br /> <br /> I don't think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3110_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3110\" data-vbnamecard=\"3110\">False Epiphany</a> posts regularly here anymore, but if he sees this he might provide more details.<br /> <br /> = = = = =<br /> I've never played Requiem myself, but I have been exposed to some of its concepts. While I have not incorporated anything wholesale into my chronicles, I have stolen bits and pieces for inclusion in my own Masquerade setting. This is what I've taken:<br /> <br /> I consider much of the Invictus to be fairly typical Camarilla stuff, so they don't exist as an organization. However, I have taken some of their etiquette, entertainment, and protocols and applied them to elder salon culture in general, or specifically to an elder only social club called Eden that has two secret Gehenna cults inside it (the Royal Order of Edenic Groundskeepers and Imperial Order of the Master Edenic Groundskeepers). I made Eden specifically so that I could introduce some of the Gehenna cults of Elysium into my setting, and parts of the Invictus sourcebook provided a lot of details and flavor I could use for it.<br /> <br /> I divided some elements of the Ordo Dracul into two places. The general &quot;we want to transcend the vampiric condition&quot; I've given to the Inconnu. It's not so much they have access to Coils, but they are exploring the same concepts. Some Inconnu individuals might have somehow gained some of those powers that overcome the curse of vampirism. That's the result of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all#post1521831\">this post here</a> where I talked about something I read in Children of the Inquisition. Some of the more general occult elements I included in a long established secret society in my chronicles where I have of non-Tremere blood sorcery users inside the Camarilla. I created that because I was tired of seemingly everyone else having some access to blood magic but the six non-Tremere clans of the Camarilla. I found some of the Ordo Dracul stuff interesting enough to provide some additional flavor to it.<br /> <br /> I used some elements of Circle of the Crone for use among Bahari. The Bahari are nowhere near in numbers of influence in my setting as the Circle of the Crone is in Requiem, but a bit more present in my chronicle than many others. Most Bahari consider themselves autarkis, but are effectively part of the Camarilla's domains. Like the Ordo Dracul, it has some good flavor text and interesting ideas I felt could be directly applied to this group.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I also incorporated some elements of the Lancea Sanctum (or Lancea et Sanctum). I established in my chronicles an organization of vampires trying to take their Christian faith seriously. This was mostly to preserve in the modern nights some elements of the Dark Ages setting which I found interesting. As most vampire culture became secular after the establishment of the Camarilla, a minority tried to preserve their medieval culture and beliefs. So some vampires who stayed on the Road of Heaven went here. This group also preserved some lore and relics from the Order of the Bitter Ash as well as elements of the Cappadocian antedeluvian's Christian beliefs like the Gospel of Laodice. They ended being one of the main sources of Noddism within the Camarilla because of that. As a result of these decisions, some of the surviving Cappadocians (and Lasombra anti-tribu) found a safe haven among this group. There are not many of these vampires, and they're not found in every domain. But they do exist as a setting element, and are a known entity even if some vampires think them odd.<br /> <br /> As such, there were certain elements of the Lancea which I selectively incorporated into this group. Much like the Bahari and the Circle of Crones, this group is much less prevalent and lack the political influence of the Lancea in the Requiem setting. This group's Christianity is certainly not the same as the Monachal faith of the Lancea, but there were things I incorporated in some fashion like some equivalent &quot;black miracles&quot; (Theban sorcery) that the group has access to. The Gospel of Laodice served as the replacement of the Testament of Longinus. Much of the role of Longinus himself was reserved for the Cappadocian antediluvian while Monachus and other black saints became other vampires, including some modified canon NPCs. Some of the darker or heretical aspects of the Sanctified faith I used for Sabbat on the Path of Night.<br /> <br /> Combined, the impact of this is probably under 20% of the setting, maybe even under 10%. I didn't move any covenants directly in my setting. I just stole a bunch of things for organizations that already existed, and was very selective about which elements I took and modified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}